WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.500
So its been basically two weeks since I pulled
my SIM from my XS Max and made the S10+ my

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.140
main device in an attempt to see how much
greener the grass is on the other side, and

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.390
let me tell you it definitely is in a lot
of ways, but it’s patchy.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.610
I’m working on my full detailed review of
the S10+ from an iPhone users perspective

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.561
so make sure to subscribe and enable notifications
so you don’t miss out, but for now, here

00:00:20.561 --> 00:00:23.010
are the biggest things that stuck out to me
so far.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.880
First off, Face ID is amazing.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:32.780
I mean I knew that before, but its definitely
much easier to use in the real world.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.370
The ultrasonic sensor is very cool, and its
really secure which you’ll know if you checked

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:43.629
out our fingerprint hack video, but man is
it flakey even after adding my thumb a second

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:48.530
time and trying intentionally lean and improve
how I use it.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:57.899
Face ID is effortless, fairly quick, and works
in apps without needing to do anything.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:01.609
Now above that ultrasonic sensor is the best
smartphone display I’ve ever put my eyes

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:02.609
on.

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:03.609
In our unboxing comparison, it didn’t seem
as bright as the XS Max, but in the real world

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:04.609
once adaptive brightness learns that you like
it turned up high it does seem brighter in

00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:05.609
direct sunlight.

00:01:05.609 --> 00:01:06.609
Along with that its definitely more detailed
in its high rez setting, and watching movies

00:01:06.609 --> 00:01:07.609
with it is fantastic, especially in HDR.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.840
Now the iPhone isn’t bad by any means, but
you do notice a difference switching back

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.930
to it, Especially if you’re streaming in
1440P on the Samsung.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.180
The speakers are really loud.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.310
After a lot of use, I don’t think they sound
as good as the iPhone, but I would take that

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:27.289
trade-off because when you’re in a loud
environment or watching a quiet video it really

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:28.289
helps.

00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:32.880
The battery powering that gorgeous display
is over 25% larger than the one in my XS Max,

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.719
but does it help in real-world use?

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:36.600
Honestly, I’m not too sure.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.259
Both of them last a full day of heavy use
but are close to dead when I go to plug them

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:41.380
in for the night.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.350
I’ll take a closer look at this in my full
review.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.549
One thing I had to change icon packs since
they are very cartoony in my opinion.

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:52.420
I also hated the way the keyboard worked and
I swapped it for the swift keyboard.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.490
I remember hearing that Apple went through
a ton of on-screen keyboard prototypes before

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.299
Steve was happy and I could I remember that
being a big thing I noticed when I bought

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:00.179
my first iPhone, the 6 Plus.

00:02:00.179 --> 00:02:05.289
In general, you have a ton of customization
and options, but it takes more effort and

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:08.940
overall I’m happy with how my iPhone works
well and gets out of the way.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.530
One thing that I’m not happy about is features
that are completely excluded in iOS as I saw

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.050
in multiple apps, the biggest one probably
being Youtubes the picture in picture mode

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.540
which is awesome for multitasking.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.890
I love and hate the notifications.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.940
On one end the S10+ and android provide much
greater looking notifications with more info

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.610
like thumbnails for youtube videos.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.650
If you Chromecast content you get constant
controls in the notifications and in general

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.640
I love having the notification bar at the
top of the phone like all android phones offer.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.500
When I get an important e-mail or text, the
icon will stay at the top until I deal with

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.500
it.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.800
This is way better for me than what iOS offers
since I'm often doing something and can’t

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.740
respond right away, but then later I just
forget about it.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.210
It doesn’t look as clean, but at a quick
glance I can see if I’m in the silent mode,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.610
if my alarm is on, and other icons.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:53.811
Along with that, I like the always on display,
and really wish Apple would include it since

00:02:53.811 --> 00:02:55.870
their flagships now use OLED displays.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:59.410
Along with those notifications differences,
we also get a lot more annoying ones that

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.080
I wasn’t used to with iOS.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.110
System notifications, downloads, and just
plain ads for apps I didn’t download like

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.110
Spotify.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:10.890
Amazon is suggesting products I should buy,
Modern combat needs reinforcements and Asphalt

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.780
9 just refueled my car lol.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.680
You can disable notifications for apps but
these are the thing I just didn’t need to

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.790
deal with before.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.330
Now let’s talk about the cameras.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:21.740
I LOVE the wide-angle lens.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:27.580
I didn’t use it that often, but when you
need its great to have and you can also get

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.060
some cool perspectives.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.690
The photos hve more contrast and saturation
than iPhones which is great if you don’t

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:33.720
like to edit.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.460
One big difference between the two is portrait
mode being wide compared to telephoto, and

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:43.430
there are plusses for both so I wish both
would give us the option to choose which lens

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.430
we wan to use.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:52.680
Samsung has made major strides in terms of
image quality and it shows.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.520
The only downside about the S10’s camera
is the shutter lag.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.420
While it does mean the images have less noise
since I often found myself missing shots of

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.780
my kids since it takes the actual photo about
noticeably after you press the shutter.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:09.270
The iPhone feels like a powerful phone for
minimalists.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.270
It just works.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.850
Yes, you have much less customization and
features, much fewer options when your taking

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.940
photos, and everything is much cleaner at
the expense of better notifications but it

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.620
just works and is less frustrating.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.640
If you own other Apple products the iPhone
is an even better device with continuity,

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.500
airplay, airdrop, etc.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.980
This has been the case for years but what
wasn’t always been the case was the hardware

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.880
quality both the materials and feel and other
things like camera and sound quality.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.200
My iPhone used to be ahead in many ways but
with the Galaxy S10 series, I feel like this

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.240
is the first time I can say that the hardware
is actually better overall.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.600
Thank you guys for watching my 2-week real
world comparison between the devices.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.920
If you have any questions go ahead and ask
in the comments section below and I’ll try

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.270
to cover them in my full detailed review of
the Galaxy S10+ and if you want to check that

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.080
out go ahead and subscribe by clicking right
up there.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.730
This has been Max with Max tech and I’ll
see you in the next video.

